<title>USA: InterCel plans $300 mln note offering.</title>
<headline>InterCel plans $300 mln note offering.</headline>
<dateline>WEST POINT, Ga. 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>InterCel Inc said Wednesday it proposes to offer $300 million of senior notes due 2007.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale are intended to be used primarily to finance certain development, construction and operating costs associated with InterCel's PCS system and to finance the first six interest payments on the notes, the company said.</p>
<p>It also said the notes have not been registered under the Securities Act of 1933, and such securities may not be offered or sold in the United States.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
</text>
